1
00:00:00,285 --> 00:00:04,790
Presentation narration: Talk Me Home is a cooperative puzzle about two incomplete views of one station.

2
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:10,545
Presentation narration: This preview uses current Practice gameplay, typed requests and exact console
confirmations.

3
00:00:10,545 --> 00:00:13,675
Presentation narration: The voice you hear is separate presentation narration.

4
00:00:13,675 --> 00:00:17,175
Presentation narration: Public hosting and current real Voice acceptance are still pending.

5
00:00:17,952 --> 00:00:21,437
Presentation narration: You sit at Mission Control with the plans and remote switches.

6
00:00:21,437 --> 00:00:24,922
Presentation narration: Pip can observe the space nearby and report what it finds.

7
00:00:24,922 --> 00:00:29,727
Presentation narration: The paper diagram is a reference. It does not reveal a live position or silently
send

8
00:00:29,727 --> 00:00:31,832
Presentation narration: your private notes to your partner.

9
00:00:32,618 --> 00:00:36,143
Presentation narration: In Cargo Bay, the Door and Conveyor share one supply.

10
00:00:36,143 --> 00:00:39,453
Presentation narration: A useful conversation turns that clue into a plan.

11
00:00:39,453 --> 00:00:44,248
Presentation narration: Pip proposes engaging the Latch. Read the exact action on the console.

12
00:00:44,248 --> 00:00:48,813
Presentation narration: Your confirmation gives the server permission to validate and perform that
specific action.

13
00:00:49,618 --> 00:00:53,493
Presentation narration: With the Latch secured, Mission Control can turn Power off.

14
00:00:53,493 --> 00:00:57,363
Presentation narration: The Conveyor stops, and the planned crossing becomes possible.

15
00:00:57,363 --> 00:01:02,633
Presentation narration: Pip proposes the crossing; you confirm it. The chapter changes only after the
server commits

16
00:01:02,633 --> 00:01:06,903
Presentation narration: the result. A spoken agreement alone does not move the robot.

17
00:01:07,685 --> 00:01:10,900
Presentation narration: The Relay Gallery makes the information gap visible.

18
00:01:10,900 --> 00:01:13,780
Presentation narration: Your atlas names the landmarks and circuits.

19
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:17,910
Presentation narration: Pencil marks are your own plan, not automatic robot tracking.

20
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:23,315
Presentation narration: Match the map with Pip's local report. Choose a circuit, ask about a passage,
and agree

21
00:01:23,315 --> 00:01:24,780
Presentation narration: on the next move.

22
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:28,985
Presentation narration: Choose the optional flight recorder objective before starting.

23
00:01:28,985 --> 00:01:34,125
Presentation narration: The archive clue points toward Leaf. Here, Pip inspects a worn case with a faded
star

24
00:01:34,125 --> 00:01:39,865
Presentation narration: and a label. Bringing it back still requires the exact Secure the flight
recorder confirmation.

25
00:01:39,865 --> 00:01:42,650
Presentation narration: A direct rescue remains a complete ending too.

26
00:01:43,452 --> 00:01:46,657
Presentation narration: A powered gate is not a promise of a clear passage.

27
00:01:46,657 --> 00:01:51,587
Presentation narration: Pip checks the way ahead. If a report contradicts your route, stop and revise
the plan

28
00:01:51,587 --> 00:01:56,732
Presentation narration: together. The console also offers a short observation request when you lose your
place,

29
00:01:56,732 --> 00:01:59,642
Presentation narration: while earlier reports keep their original chapter.

30
00:02:00,452 --> 00:02:06,622
Presentation narration: At Return Dock, the roles meet again. Pip holds the contact after your exact
confirmation.

31
00:02:06,622 --> 00:02:10,697
Presentation narration: Mission Control charges the supply and moves that energy into storage.

32
00:02:10,697 --> 00:02:15,837
Presentation narration: Storage retains energy for the return. The procedure still needs a safe release,
boarding

33
00:02:15,837 --> 00:02:18,052
Presentation narration: and a separate return authorization.

34
00:02:18,885 --> 00:02:23,665
Presentation narration: Pip releases the contact and boards the capsule, one confirmed action at a time.

35
00:02:23,665 --> 00:02:26,580
Presentation narration: Only then can Mission Control grant the return.

36
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:29,755
Presentation narration: The final proposal is checked against the current state.

37
00:02:29,755 --> 00:02:34,090
Presentation narration: Confirmed home is a game result, rather than a promise made in conversation.

38
00:02:34,885 --> 00:02:39,850
Presentation narration: The station is behind you. Pip is home, and the case you chose to recover has a
place

39
00:02:39,850 --> 00:02:44,275
Presentation narration: on the shelf. The arrival artwork celebrates a verified ending.

40
00:02:44,275 --> 00:02:48,390
Presentation narration: This scene is an actual current Practice completion, with no provider connection
and no

41
00:02:48,390 --> 00:02:50,410
Presentation narration: claim of a human playtest.

42
00:02:51,185 --> 00:02:55,510
Presentation narration: Voice mode uses browser audio and the AssemblyAI Voice Agent API.

43
00:02:55,510 --> 00:02:59,810
Presentation narration: Local function requests pass through the browser to an authoritative game
server.

44
00:02:59,810 --> 00:03:04,685
Presentation narration: Raw captions preserve what was said. Private map marks remain with the human.

45
00:03:04,685 --> 00:03:08,840
Presentation narration: Physical actions still require exact confirmation and a current state check.

46
00:03:09,618 --> 00:03:13,178
Presentation narration: This is a working preview, not current Live acceptance.

47
00:03:13,178 --> 00:03:18,428
Presentation narration: Public HTTPS access, the Voice acceptance pair and final media are pending.

48
00:03:18,428 --> 00:03:21,743
Presentation narration: Source remains private pending historical disclosure.

49
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:25,043
Presentation narration: Earlier Voice success and failure records stay separate.

50
00:03:25,043 --> 00:03:29,228
Presentation narration: The finished release will report its actual hosted result and ending
acknowledgement.
